'''Grasping wind''' is an wind-type [[Spells|spell]] that causes a strong wind current towards the glyph.

==Description==
Grasping wind contains a wind sigil surrounded by inward facing pulling signs. When completed, this spell will cause a wind current to go towards it, having enough force to pull some lighter objects towards it. Additionally, if the pulling signs are slanted, the air will twist, creating a vortex that can twist objects as they are pulled towards the spell.{{Ref|m|14|3}}

==Usage==
The spell was first seen being used by [[Coco]] when she was attempting to use the spell to pluck a [[Mountain Apple|mountain apple]] from a small tree, but she drew the glyph too large and uprooted the entire tree.{{Ref|m|14|2}} [[Tetia]] suggested drawing the keystones at an angle to create a small vortex and pluck out the apples more easily.{{Ref|m|14|3}} [[Agott]] then made the same spell, but managed to preform it perfectly, retrieving the fruit while leaving the tree unharmed.{{Ref|m|14|4-5}} 

During the events of [[The Sincerity of the Shield]] test, [[Agott]] used the spell to capture a [[Myrphon|myrphon]] who was attempting to run off,{{Ref|m|20}} and Coco managed to successfully use this spell to take a magic necklace from the hands of [[Iguin]]. 

